//BUG="a function may declare the same parameter name twice"
//ERR any

// `parse_function_declaration` (src/compiler/parser/function.rs) collects
// parameters without comparing their names, and `normalize_function`
// registers each one with `SymbolTable::new_variable`, where a later name
// simply replaces an earlier one. The declaration below is accepted, the
// first argument becomes unreachable, and the program prints 2.
//
// The same repetition is an error for the fields of a struct
// (08_structs/71e_a_field_declared_twice.cpl, "Field … declared twice"), and
// here it can only be a typo: nothing can name the first parameter, so no
// program means to write this.
//
// There is no `//MSG` because the diagnostic does not exist yet. Template
// parameters have the same gap — `fn f[T T] x: T` is accepted too.

fn pick a a
    ret a

fn main
    out "{pick(1 2)}"
